 <p class="wp-block-paragraph">Two-thirds of Canton public school students had their school day disrupted Monday due to an electrical issue at the city’s water treatment plant.</p>
 <p class="wp-block-paragraph">Canton Municipal Utilities <a href="https://www.facebook.com/permalink.php?story_fbid=pfbid0zVvmg76dPhqxTaZ6bV85EEnueQLaSTuakBnGqCQYFZ3bovU6i7eWGC3iPK8obuqCl&amp;id=100064330742874&amp;rdid=SxD7iTTJpbfwMH8W">announced Monday</a> on social media that an electrical issue at a water treatment plant resulted in a loss of water services and reduced water pressure in some parts of Canton. The issue was resolved, according to the statement, and water service and pressure should return to normal.</p>
 <p class="wp-block-paragraph">The water issue affected four school buildings — Huey Porter Middle, Canton High, Goodloe Elementary and Canton Elementary — comprising more than 2,000 students of the district’s 3,137 total enrollment.</p>
